      <Comment>Lactate, or 2-hydroxypropanoate, was discovered in 1780 by the Swedish chemist Scheele, who isolated it from sour milk. It is the simplest hydroxycarboxylic acid and exists as 2 stereoisomers. Lactate has a pK of 3.86 and exists at a lactate ion:|FRAME: CPD-24845| ratio of 3000:1 at physiological pH |CITS: [15987839]|.</Comment>
